# Per-host settings for the Klaud Kode API. Copy to "env" and edit.
# Every line is optional; the defaults work for a plain setup.
#
# This file is sourced by the shell, so quote any value containing spaces:
#   KOMPUTER_BODY_NAME="my Windows desktop"

# Release binary handling (start.sh downloads a checksum-verified release).
# Pin a version, reuse an existing binary, or build from this checkout instead.
#KLAUD_KODE_VERSION=v1.0.1
#KLAUD_KODE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/klaud-kode
#KLAUD_KODE_BUILD=1

# Where Claude Code is, if it is not on PATH.
#CLAUDE_BIN=/home/you/.local/bin/claude
#NODE_BIN=/home/you/.nvm/versions/node/v22/bin/node

# CLI backends, routed by the request's model name (see docs/backends.md).
# The default "claude" is the original Claude-only service.
#KOMPUTER_BACKENDS=claude,antigravity,muse
#KOMPUTER_DEFAULT_BACKEND=claude
#AGY_BIN=/home/you/.local/bin/agy
#MUSE_BIN=/home/you/.local/bin/muse
#KOMPUTER_AGY_MODELS=komputer-gemini-4-argon,komputer-gemini-3.8-flash
# Other agy models use a komputer-agy- prefix, e.g. komputer-agy-claude-opus-5-5.
#KOMPUTER_AGY_MODEL=
#KOMPUTER_AGY_TASK_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash-low
# Gemini rejects xhigh/max; higher requests clamp to the top of this list.
#KOMPUTER_AGY_EFFORTS=low,medium,high
# agy reads MCP servers only from ~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json. "auto"
# registers a stdio bridge there per MCP name with `agy mcp add` at startup
# (no URLs or tokens are written); "off" only logs the command to run.
#KOMPUTER_AGY_MCP_SETUP=auto
# "off": like Claude, agy's own tools (run_command, read_file, ...) are denied by
# a PreToolUse hook in ~/.gemini/config/hooks.json and the model reaches the
# user's computer through komputer_use. Experimental, POSIX Bodies only (a
# Windows Body stays on "off"): commands through a bash shim on agy's PATH, files
# through a FUSE mount of the Body root ("auto": when fuse3 + python3-fusepy are
# here; "all": required; "commands": file tools denied). See docs/backends.md.
#KOMPUTER_AGY_REMOTE_TOOLS=off
# Shell for remote commands when the redirect is on (default bash).
#KOMPUTER_AGY_REMOTE_SHELL=
#KOMPUTER_AGY_REMOTE_MOUNT=/srv/komputer-work-agy/remote
#KOMPUTER_AGY_PYTHON=python3
# Backstop for a tool step that still acted on THIS host: "warn" logs it,
# "stop" ends the turn (502 builtin_tool_blocked), "off" does not check.
#KOMPUTER_AGY_BUILTIN_GUARD=warn
# "settings" relies on agy's own permissions; allow "mcp(komputer_use/*)" and,
# for remote commands, "command(*)" in ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json.
# "skip" passes --dangerously-skip-permissions; the hook then limits agy's tools.
#KOMPUTER_AGY_PERMISSIONS=settings
#KOMPUTER_MUSE_MODELS=
#KOMPUTER_MUSE_MODEL=
# Extra CLI arguments, split on whitespace (no quoting).
#KOMPUTER_AGY_EXTRA_ARGS=
#KOMPUTER_MUSE_EXTRA_ARGS=
#KOMPUTER_AGY_CWD=/srv/komputer-work-agy
#KOMPUTER_MUSE_CWD=/srv/komputer-work-muse

# Stored /v1/responses replies for previous_response_id. Empty = memory only.
#KOMPUTER_RESPONSES_FILE=
#KOMPUTER_MAX_STORED_RESPONSES=1000

# Listen address. Add a second entry to also serve another port, e.g.
# KOMPUTER_API_HOST=127.0.0.1,127.0.0.1:8317
#KOMPUTER_API_HOST=127.0.0.1
#KOMPUTER_API_PORT=18888

# Public HTTPS access to this service (not a model-provider API key).
#KOMPUTER_PUBLIC_API=1
#KOMPUTER_API_HOST=0.0.0.0
#KOMPUTER_TLS_CERT_FILE=/etc/komputer/tls/fullchain.pem
#KOMPUTER_TLS_KEY_FILE=/etc/komputer/tls/privkey.pem
# Only for an encrypted PKCS#8 key (`openssl genpkey` default):
#KOMPUTER_TLS_KEY_PASSPHRASE=
#KOMPUTER_DEPLOY_HEALTH_URL=https://api.example.com:18888/healthz
# For an HTTP backend reachable ONLY by a trusted TLS proxy, explicit opt-in:
#KOMPUTER_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=1
# Browser origins only; native harnesses do not need CORS configuration.
#KOMPUTER_CORS_ORIGINS=https://harness.example.com,http://localhost:3000
#KOMPUTER_AUTH_FAILURE_LIMIT=20
#KOMPUTER_MAX_CONNECTIONS=512

# Client-tool mode waits for local results without holding a compute slot.
#KOMPUTER_CLIENT_TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
#KOMPUTER_MAX_CLIENT_TOOL_RUNS=16

# Outbound proxy for Claude Code, if this host needs one. Leave unset if not.
#HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
#HTTP_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7890
#NO_PROXY=127.0.0.1,localhost,::1,*.ts.net,100.64.0.0/10

# How the workstation is described to Claude, and the MCP server name in .mcp.json.
#KOMPUTER_BODY_NAME="my Windows desktop"
#KOMPUTER_BODY_MCP=komputer_use

# Working note appended to Claude Code's system prompt. It only says where the
# user's files and shell are. Replace it, or set it empty for no note at all:
#KOMPUTER_SYSTEM_PROMPT=""

# Reaching the body over a virtual private network (Tailscale, ZeroTier,
# WireGuard): give its MCP URL and the .mcp.json is generated from it. No ssh
# tunnel and no BODY_SSH are used. Put the body token in the URL path, or in
# KOMPUTER_BODY_TOKEN to keep it out of the URL.
#KOMPUTER_BODY_URL=http://100.64.0.8:8787/mcp/YOUR_BODY_TOKEN
#KOMPUTER_BODY_TOKEN=
# Health probe for that URL; default replaces /mcp with /healthz.
#KOMPUTER_BODY_PROBE=http://100.64.0.8:8787/healthz

# Alternative: the Body dials out to this server (best for a computer behind
# home NAT or on another continent). No inbound to that machine is needed.
# KOMPUTER_BODY_TOKEN above authenticates the link.
#KOMPUTER_BODY_CONNECT=1

# Alternative: the body, as ssh sees it (used by komputer/tunnel-up.sh when no
# KOMPUTER_BODY_URL is set).
#BODY_SSH=body
#LOCAL_PORT=18787
#BODY_PORT=8787

# Health probe for the body, and the script that revives the tunnel.
#KOMPUTER_HEALTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18787/healthz
#KOMPUTER_TUNNEL_UP=/path/to/komputer/tunnel-up.sh
# Set to 1 when the brain and the body are the same machine.
#KOMPUTER_SKIP_TUNNEL=0
# Failed probe/revive backoff in milliseconds (0 disables it). Success cache: 15s.
#KOMPUTER_TUNNEL_FAIL_CACHE_MS=30000

# Extra child environment names, comma-separated and exact. Only add trusted
# runtime configuration; values become visible to Claude and its subprocesses.
# KOMPUTER_*, BODY_*, KLAUD_KODE_* and launcher settings stay excluded.
#KOMPUTER_CHILD_ENV_EXTRA=CLAUDE_CODE_PROJECT_DIR_NAME
# Certificate, CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, MCP timeout, shell,
# telemetry and proxy variables are already allowed. Upper/lowercase proxy
# names work; no proxy is invented when absent. ALL_PROXY forwarding does not
# guarantee support by every Claude Code networking component.
# Existing ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN remain supported; unset the
# API key if you intend to use subscription login (the API logs a warning).

# Island mode (L2) is on by default: --tools "" removes all built-in tools.
#KOMPUTER_BUILTIN_TOOLS=default
# Empty non-git dir for Claude's cwd. The default is a stable per-installation
# directory under ~/.komputer/workspaces/, outside the application checkout.
#KOMPUTER_CLAUDE_CWD=/srv/komputer-work
# Experimental full system-prompt replacement. Evaluate on the brain first.
# A missing/unreadable file or a directory causes startup to fail.
# Relative paths are resolved from the API process's startup directory.
#KOMPUTER_SYSTEM_PROMPT_FILE=/path/to/island-prompt.txt
